#### 3. Trivial `IsNotNull` Assertions (3 tests)

| Line | Method | Problem |
|------|--------|---------|
| 25 | `GetProduct_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` — never checks SKU, name, or price match |
| 46 | `SearchProducts_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` — never checks the list contains "Widget" or has correct count |
| 55 | `GetAllProducts_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` — never checks the list has 1 item |

These pass even if the returned object has completely wrong data. `IsNotNull` on a `List<T>` is especially hollow — an empty list is also not null.

**Fix** — assert on the content:

```csharp
// GetProduct_Works → GetProduct_ReturnsMatchingProduct
var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(result);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", result.Sku);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);

// SearchProducts_Works → Search_ByName_ReturnsMatchingProducts
var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);

// GetAllProducts_Works → GetAll_ReturnsAllAddedProducts
var all = _catalog.GetAll();
Assert.AreEqual(1, all.Count);
```

